The analysis of the impact of colonization on a country such as PNG, then, poses a large number of fundamental theoretical problems. The particular problems that this book addresses itself to can be summarized as follows. First, there is a need to develop a general conceptual framework within which a distinction between capitalist and noncapitalist economies can be made. Secondly, a set of concepts for describing the basic features of the indigenous economy of PNG, as well as a system for classifying the different types of indigenous economic systems in PNG, is required. Thirdly, these concepts must be able to generate propositions to account for the historical and anthropological data on the impact of colonization on PNG and, in particular, the efflorescence of the indigenous economy.
