HONG KONG, Oct. 1 -- Caterpillar Inc. announced the appointment Tuesday of a new independently owned dealership in Ulan Bator, Mongolia, which will be owned by shareholders of Wagner Equipment Corp. of Aurora, Colo. Wagner Equipment has been the Caterpillar dealer for Colorado since 1974.

The Mongolia People's Republic with a population of 2.4 million offers market opportunities in mining, construction, agriculture and electric power generation. Since 1992, Caterpillar has been providing direct coverage in Mongolia through an office, warehouse and service facility there. The agreement, effective immediately, authorizes the dealership to perform all the traditional functions of a Caterpillar dealer, including prime product and parts sales, delivery and warranty service, customer training and after-sales support. Caterpillar Inc., headquartered in Peoria, Ill., is the world's largest manufacturer of earth-moving and construction equipment, gas engines and industrial gas turbines. It is a leading global suplier of diesel engines and its recorded sales and revenues in 1995 came to more than $16 billion.

