The TAKE IT DOWN Act criminalizes the publication of nonconsensual intimate visual depictions. It also requires covered platforms to: (1) create a process for consumers to notify covered platforms of a nonconsensual intimate visual depiction on the platform; and (2) remove such depictions within 48 hours of receiving notice. The FTC is charged with enforcing this notice and removal process.

