[2] Mac Mouse Alternative for Tremor, Arthritis, Shaky Hands
URL: https://inputconfig.com/guides/tremor-and-limited-range
The best mouse alternative for tremor on a Mac is often a game controller stick, because a stick can ignore a shake that a mouse has to follow. macOS has no tremor filter of its own, and SteadyMouse, the best-known anti-tremor app, is Windows software. InputConfig makes a controller stick the mouse, with settings a mouse does not have: a deadzone that swallows the shake, a slow curve, and a click that waits for the hand to settle.

This guide is for hands that shake or do not reach far: essential tremor, Parkinson's, arthritis, an injury, or plain tiredness late in the day. It covers two problems with numbers to start from. A tremor means the stick shakes around wherever the thumb rests, so the pointer jitters and clicks land off target. Limited range means the stick never reaches the edge, so the pointer never reaches full speed. Allow half an hour with the person beside you. The Steady Pointer preset on this page has the starting numbers built in.
...
, Slow Keys, Dwell ... and Voice Control
...
1. Tracking speed. Mouse, or Trackpad. A slower pointer turns a shake into a smaller movement.
2. Slow Keys. Accessibility, Keyboard. A key has to be held for a moment before it counts, so a brushed or bounced key does not type.
3. Dwell. Search for Dwell in System Settings. Resting the pointer for a set time clicks, so no button is pressed at all.
4. Mouse Keys. Accessibility, Pointer Control. The pointer moves from the keyboard instead of the hand.
5. Voice Control. Accessibility, Voice Control. Clicks, menus, and typing by voice.

If those are enough, you are done. If the pointer itself is still the problem, move it to a controller stick, where a shake can be ignored instead of followed.
...
