# I’m continuing to run demos of Parkinsonic and show how our system works —from symptom assessment (voice, speech, movement, tremor) to adaptive therapeutic music. · 2026-02-02T00:00:00+00:00

I’m continuing to run demos of Parkinsonic and show how our system works —from symptom assessment (voice, speech, movement, tremor) to adaptive therapeutic music.
...
> Parkinsonic is an AI-powered digital health platform for people with Parkinson’s disease that combines symptom assessment and personalized therapeutic music in one continuous loop.
>
> How it works:
> We start with a digital symptom assessment, capturing key biomarkers related to Parkinson’s — including voice, speech patterns, movement, and tremor.
> These signals help us understand the current motor and functional state of a person.
>
> Based on this assessment, our system generates and adapts music in real time — adjusting rhythm, tempo, structure, and intensity to support movement, regulation, and focus.
>
> Music is not used as background, but as an active, responsive therapeutic layer.
>
> If you’d like to explore it yourself:
> / You can try our interactive demo on the Parkinsonic website and see how assessment and music generation work together
> / You can listen to example tracks from our system on Bandcamp to understand the therapeutic sound direction
>
> We are open to collaborations with digital health, neurotech, and wearable projects that work with biometric or movement data and could benefit from an adaptive music engine integrated into their product or therapy flow.
>
