A PCI non-compliance fee is a monthly charge that a business's acquiring bank or payments provider adds when that business hasn't completed the PCI DSS validation its merchant agreement requires. 

Different businesses have different validation requirements. Card networks sort businesses into four levels based on annual transaction volume: a business processing millions of transactions a year faces stricter documentation than one processing a few thousand. Businesses that handle card data directly on their own servers carry more compliance responsibility than those routing payment fields through a hosted or tokenised solution, since the scope of what needs auditing shifts with each setup.
