The NEPSY-II is an updated tool for assessing neuropsychological development in children aged 3 to 16, incorporating a range of subtests across various cognitive domains. While it maintains robust utility in evaluating neuropsychological functioning and supports intervention planning, certain subtests lack current reliability data, warranting conservative interpretation. Comprehensive understanding and effective administration of the NEPSY-II require a substantial foundation in neuropsychological principles and may pose challenges for practitioners.

