## What This Means for Manicurists and Pedicurists in Pennsylvania

 According to BLS OEWS state estimates, Pennsylvania ranks #46 of 50 states and territories for Manicurists and Pedicurists pay, the bottom 9% nationally. Full pay-distribution context, including how Pennsylvania compares to the national median, follows below. 

 This page captures the Manicurists and Pedicurists labor market inside Pennsylvania using BLS Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics state estimates from the May 2025 release. Median annual pay lands at $27,990 ($13.46/hr per hour), while the state employs roughly 9,610 workers in this SOC code (39-5092). Relative to the national median of $35,760, the state estimate is 22% below. Explaining that difference would require separate evidence on industry, employer, prices, and worker mix. 

 Within Pennsylvania, the full pay distribution is wider than the median alone suggests. Workers at the 10th percentile earn $20,520, the 25th earns $21,510, the 75th reaches $33,180, and the 90th hits $43,890. The upper boundary is roughly 2.1× the lower boundary. These bands combine workers across experience levels, credentials, employers, industries, schedules, and specialties; the percentile table does not isolate any one factor's effect. 

 Use this state-level view as one layer in your research stack…

