The credential in this guide is the Pennsylvania nail technician license, a limited license under the Cosmetology Law. Statutory language still says manicurist. On this path, nail technician and manicurist name the same limited license. They do not name the full cosmetologist license. The examination is the Theory/Procedural Skills Examination of the Pennsylvania State Board of Cosmetology. Pearson VUE creates that examination and scores it.
...
A theoretical item asks what a rule, a nail structure, or a product fact means. A procedural skill item is still a multiple-choice question. It asks which step comes next, which product fits the service, or which method keeps the client safe. The computer presents both kinds of items in one sitting. The Pearson VUE Pennsylvania cosmetology FAQ describes an approximate 50/50 split between theoretical and procedural skill items. This license has no hands-on practical examination. You will not perform a manicure on a model, set up a stati…

