religious landscape of Hellenistic Greek poleis, one field of action for Aphrodite is the protection of magistracies. A specific aspect of the “Aphrodite of the magistrates” can be identified in the relationship established by the strategoi, public officials entrusted with significant political and military powers. This article presents the collection of the epigraphic dossier concerning the “strategic” cults of Aphrodite. The interpretation of the sources considers the manner in which the cultic actors built their communication with the patron goddess. Specifically, the article analyzes the onomastic attributes, rather specialized and distinctive, that the strategoi chose to assign to Aphrodite, revealing a functional mirroring dynamic (Strategis, Strateia, Hegemone). At the same time, divine configurations shaped by the worshippers are investigated, in which Aphrodite is placed in dialogue with other deities, primarily Zeus.
