URL: https://www.ylytic.com/home/new/blog/blog-instagram-benchmarks-2026
Instagram's engagement story in 2025 was one of structural decline at the platform average but clear opportunity in specific formats and markets. Socialinsider's analysis of 35 million posts from 447,613 pages across January–December 2025 found the overall average engagement rate settled at 0.48% — a 24% year-on-year drop. [1] Yet the story beneath that headline is far more nuanced — and far more actionable for 2026.
...
Engagement rate (ER) methodology matters enormously for interpretation. The Socialinsider 2025 benchmark (0.48% average) uses follower-based ER: (likes + comments) ÷ followers × 100. Buffer's analysis of 2M+ posts using a slightly broader methodology found a median of 4.3%. Qoruz's India-specific research found nano-influencers hitting 4–6% regularly. [1][4][5] These are not contradictory — they reflect different account sizes, methodologies, and markets.
