### Reach rate by brand size on Facebook and Instagram

Not every page is playing the same game. A brand-new account with a couple thousand followers and an established page with a million followers see very different reach, purely because of how the reach rate math works. 

Here's what that looks like in practice:

| Brand size | Instagram reach rate | Facebook reach rate |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1-5K | 6.65% | 4.35% |
| 5-10K | 5.75% | 3.40% |
| 10-50K | 5.50% | 2.70% |
| 50-100K | 4.50% | 1.50% |
| 100K - 1M | 3.50% | 0.50% |

And the takeaway here is that the smaller the page, the bigger the slice of its audience it reaches. On Instagram, pages in the 1-5K bracket pull a 6.65% reach rate, nearly double what pages in the 100K-1M range see. Facebook's drop-off is even sharper, falling from 4.35% for the smallest pages to just 0.50% for the biggest ones.

Instagram also drives roughly 2x more reach than Facebook at almost every size bracket, and the gap only widens as pages get bigger.
