The app’s continued growth in India is also fueled by increasing smartphone adoption, affordable data, and the popularity of Reels and regional content. With a diverse user base spanning across age groups, regions, and languages, Instagram has evolved into more than just a social networking platform — it’s become a hub for discovery, digital commerce, and brand interaction. As more Indian users turn to Instagram for news, trends, and entertainment, it remains a critical platform for marketers aiming to connect with Gen Z and millennial audiences in the country.
