Rationale 
Syncope is a common presentation to the emergency department (ED) that accounts for 1% to 1.5% of 
ED annual visits and up to 6% of hospital admissions. Patients with only low-risk characteristics and 
without any high-risk characteristics can be classified as low risk and can be safely discharged from the 
ED. These patients do not need further diagnostic tests in the ED and their likely diagnosis is reflex, 
situational, or orthostatic syncope. Low-risk patients may still require further examination or…

