(Ackermans et al., 2012; Lobodzinski & Laks, 2012;
Locati, 2002; Zimetbaum & Goldman, 2010; Zimetbaum,
Kim, Josephson, Goldberger, & Cohen, 1998). Optimal
electrode application includes the following: (1) shaving
the skin if necessary; (2) removing dead skin cells by
rubbing the area with a rough paper or cloth; (3) using
electrodes from air tight packages; and (4) paying attention
to expiration dates on the electrodes packages (Kligﬁeld
et al., 2007).

