Table 3 provides guidance on which patients require hospital admission with the remainder being managed more conservatively [3]. If the diagnosis remains elusive, the ideal approach is for a syncope specialist to see the patient, with a rate of diagnosis of 90% [13]. This is Phase 3, but it is unrealistic to think that a syncope specialist is available in every ED 24 h per day as there are too few of them. When an attempt at diagnosis is made, the rate of diagnoses improves [20].

