By default, jobs run in stages. All jobs in a stage must finish successfully before any job in a later stage can start. For example, with the default `build`, `test`, and `deploy` stages, all jobs in `build` must run and finish before any job in `test` can start.

With `needs`, you list specific jobs a job depends on. The job starts immediately after those dependencies finish, even if other jobs in earlier stages are still running. This creates a pipeline with a kind of directed acyclic graph (DAG) structure.
