GitLab supports both manually triggered and timed rollouts to a Kubernetes production system using Incremental Rollouts. When using Manual Rollouts, the release of each tranche of pods is manually triggered. With Timed Rollouts, the release is performed in tranches after a default pause of 5 minutes. Timed rollouts can also be manually triggered before the pause period has expired.

Manual and Timed rollouts are included automatically in projects controlled by Auto DevOps, but they are also configurable through GitLab CI/CD in the `.gitlab-ci.yml` configuration file.

Manually triggered rollouts can be implemented with Continuous Delivery, while timed rollouts do not require intervention and can be part of your Continuous Deployment strategy. You can also combine both of them in a way that the app is deployed automatically unless you eventually intervene manually if necessary.
