The usage of instance runners by projects running CI/CD jobs is measured in compute minutes.
...
- The base monthly compute quota is determined by your subscription tier. Free tier namespaces receive 400 compute minutes per month. Paid tiers receive a higher monthly quota.
- You can purchase additional compute minutes if you need more.
...
The cost factor is a multiplier that sets how quickly a job uses compute minutes. It is not a monetary price. The rate varies based on the runner type and project settings.
...
### Project type discounts

Certain discounts apply based on the project type:

| Project type | Cost factor | Compute minutes used |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Standard projects | Based on runner type | 1 minute per (job duration / 60 × cost factor) |
| Public projects in the GitLab for Open Source program | `0.5` | 1 minute per 2 minutes of job time |
| Public forks of projects in the GitLab for Open Source program | `0.008` | 1 minute per 125 minutes of job time |
| Community contributions | Dynamic discount | See the following section |
...
The cost factor calculation is:

- `Monthly compute quota / 300,000 job duration minutes = Cost factor`

For example, with a monthly compute quota of 10,000 in the Premium tier:

- 10,000 / 300,000 = 0.03333333333 cost factor.

